e article among multiple similarly dated results.\nI’ll fetch Universe Today’s June 2023 archive page directly and identify the June 6 entry from the page content.\nI’ll extract only primitive summary fields from the archive response in the same execution, accommodating either list- or dictionary-shaped search output.\nI’m making one targeted scholarly search for the paper’s title and funding acknowledgment; this should provide the award number directly if the article link is indexed.\nI’ll broaden the funding-number search across 2023 astronomy papers coauthored by Arendt, then cross-check the resulting paper against Universe Today’s June 6 article.\nI’ll query Universe Today’s WordPress feed for posts published on June 6, then follow the matching post’s outbound paper link and extract the acknowledgment text programmatically.\nI’m using the article’s likely phrasing plus the paper-author clue to identify the exact publication independently of the archive endpoint.\nI’ll run the archive-to-paper extraction in one pass, searching each June 6 post for outbound arXiv/DOI links and then scanning the linked paper for “Arendt” and “NASA award.”\nThe paper linked in Carolyn Collins Petersen’s June 6, 2023 Universe Today article is the team’s observational study referenced at the article’s conclusion. In its acknowledgments, it states that R. G. Arendt’s work was supported by NASA award number 80NSSC20K0644.']
